+# Recovered March 2012 request and review-record addendum
+
+October 25, 2026. Added under the user’s explicit public-publication request. M132–M134 append to the preserved 131-entry compilation.
+
+- [March 19, 2012 request](https://www.ae911truth.org/images/PDFs/LTR20120319RHB.pdf): four-page public scan, all ten questions; SHA-256 `fd712bc4361b3042bc9e5b41b4193c3d39fc1b4dc4c830f3cd1e8704f8cfcb5d`; 198178 bytes.
+- [Appeal packet](https://www.ae911truth.org/images/PDFs/DOC-NIST-2014-001436_Appeal.pdf): 29-page public scan; request at physical pp9–12, Exhibit E; response begins at p13, Exhibit F; SHA-256 `d3cb27dbb8330858e2feb6491e0c4adce2fe1f7abdd0c1f52457d61b1ccddb00`; 1545570 bytes.
+
+The June 27 reply acknowledges March 26 receipt and attributes two FAQs and two typographical corrections to the questions. It announces updated errata availability on June 28. This is evidence of notice and a public correction response, not proof that NIST accepted the objections, reran a model, knew a correction prevented collapse or concealed an adverse result. Publication date and next-day availability remain distinct observations.
+
+## All ten question topics
+
+These are the requester’s topics and assertions, not adopted engineering findings.
+
+1. Studs and the floor 13 girder.
+2. Drawing revisions, added studs/plates and corresponding floor loads.
+3. Drawing 1091 bearing plate: 12 inches versus printed 11 inches.
+4. Drawing 9114 stiffeners in the partial-floor representation.
+5. Restraint at columns 44/79 and walk-off/rocking.
+6. Possible walk-off mode versus listed partial-floor observations.
+7. Northern W21x44 beam and three W12x19 bracing members.
+8. How lateral walk-off was measured/monitored.
+9. Stiffeners, residual support and the request’s 5.5-inch displacement argument.
+10. Quantitative Case B 4.0-hour shapes, rotations, temperatures and axial forces.
+
+The request’s earlier dimensions and assertions remain attributed to that request; later errata are not silently substituted. The two request reproductions share a documentary lineage. Public scans, a printed reply and a reproduced signature do not provide native-email or agency custody authentication.
+
+## Still missing
+
+The actual STENG-2119/R1 submissions, complete reviewer reports, response-to-reviewers, submission/revision receipts and original editor decisions remain unlocated in the cited bounded search. The later author account identifies and partly quotes them; it is not the full journal file. The published October 2012 discussion is not relabeled as either submitted version without an authenticated join. Search failures establish neither suppression nor nonexistence.
+
+## Verification and preservation
+
+Publication preparation rechecked the two scan hashes and research-report hash, confirmed four and 29 physical pages, and visually inspected all four request pages plus appeal page13 using previously rendered originals on the verified media store. The source study reports 90 passing preservation checks; that whole study was not rerun here. No raw scan, signature, personal/contact details, private case file or native email is uploaded. Public source URLs, hashes, page locators and selected technical findings are retained.
